{
  "extends": "expo/tsconfig.base",
  "compilerOptions": {},

  /*
   * THIS FILE COMPILES NOTHING, ON PURPOSE.
   *
   * Every buildable thing in the repo owns its own project and extends
   * `expo/tsconfig.base` itself — apps/rider, apps/driver and apps/admin each
   * declare their own `paths`, and apps/admin's `@/*` alias exists nowhere else.
   * The shared `packages/*` are consumed as SOURCE through those aliases, so
   * they are only meaningful when type-checked inside a consuming app, which is
   * why none of them has a tsconfig either.
   *
   * With no `files`/`include`, this config defaulted to `**\/*` and swallowed
   * the whole tree: a bare `tsc` at the repo root reported hundreds of errors
   * that no build has — "Cannot find module '@/lib/api'" for admin code that
   * type-checks clean, React Native style errors against `packages/ui` compiled
   * without RN's lib, and a second copy of every file from the stale, git-
   * ignored `eyego/` duplicate nested inside the repo (which on Windows also
   * produced the "differs only in casing" noise). Nothing in package.json ran
   * it, so the trap sat waiting for whoever tried `tsc` first.
   *
   * Type-check per project:
   *   tsc --noEmit -p apps/rider
   *   tsc --noEmit -p apps/driver
   *   tsc --noEmit -p apps/admin
   */
  "files": [],
  "include": []
}
